<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Günther Victor, Prince of Schwarzburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a>–<a href="/years/1925">1925</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Günther Viktor of Schwarzburg-Rudolstadt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Günther Victor was Prince of Schwarzburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolstadt">Rudolstadt</a> from 1890 and, after the death of his cousin in 1909, also of Schwarzburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sondershausen">Sondershausen</a>, ruling the two states in personal union. He abdicated in November 1918 for Rudolstadt and Sondershausen, among the last German monarchs to give up their thrones. Both principalities joined the Free State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> in 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gunther-victor-prince-of-schwarzburg.jpg" alt="Günther Victor, Prince of Schwarzburg" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Reichard &amp; Lindner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%BCnther_Victor_von_Schwarzburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
